.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt AR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ar
.Nd create and change archives of object files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo Fl Oc Ns Ar operation Ns Op Ar modifiers
.Op Ar relpos
.Op Ar count
.Ar archive
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
keeps a set of files in one archive, usually object files for the
linker.
When the archive has object files, it also writes an index of the symbols
they define, so the linker finds them; for Mach-O objects the archive is
in Darwin's format.
.Pp
The operation is one of these letters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm d
Delete the
.Ar file Ns s
from the archive.
.It Cm m
Move the
.Ar file Ns s
to the end, or next to
.Ar relpos
with
.Cm a ,
.Cm b
or
.Cm i .
.It Cm p
Write the contents of the
.Ar file Ns s ,
or of every member, to the standard output.
.It Cm q
Append the
.Ar file Ns s
without looking for members of the same name.
.It Cm r
Replace the members named like the
.Ar file Ns s ,
or add them.
.It Cm s
Only write the symbol index, as
.Xr ranlib 1 .
.It Cm t
List the members.
.It Cm x
Extract the
.Ar file Ns s ,
or every member.
.El
.Pp
The modifiers are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm a , b , i
Put the files after
.Pq Cm a
or before
.Pq Cm b , i
the member
.Ar relpos .
.It Cm c
Do not say so when the archive has to be created.
.It Cm D
Write zero for dates, user and group (the default), so that the same
input gives the same archive.
.It Cm N
With several members of the same name, use the
.Ar count Ns th.
.It Cm o
When extracting, keep the members' dates.
.It Cm O
With
.Cm t ,
show each member's offset.
.It Cm P
Match members by their full path.
.It Cm s
Write the symbol index too.
.It Cm S
Do not write a symbol index.
.It Cm u
With
.Cm r ,
only replace members older than the files.
.It Cm U
Write the real dates, user and group.
.It Cm v
Say what is done; with
.Cm t ,
list modes, sizes and dates as well.
.El
.Pp
Other options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -format Ns = Ns Ar format
Write the archive in
.Ar format :
.Cm darwin ,
.Cm bsd ,
.Cm gnu
or
.Cm default ,
chosen from the members.
.It Fl -output Ns = Ns Ar dir
Extract into
.Ar dir .
.It Fl -thin
Make a thin archive, which only names the files.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make a static library and list it:
.Dl ar rcs libdemo.a a.o b.o
.Dl ar tv libdemo.a
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ranlib 1 ,
.Xr size 1 ,
.Xr strings 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is LLVM's llvm-ar.
